THIRD-PARTY CODE
================

This repository contains and builds upon third-party code, which remains under
its own license. A copy of the Apache License 2.0 is included as
LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.

* SMDM -- "Scaling up Masked Diffusion Models on Text" (Nie et al., 2025),
  https://github.com/ML-GSAI/SMDM, Apache-2.0.
  This repository started as a fork of SMDM. `lit_gpt/`, `pretrain/train_ar.py`,
  `pretrain/train_mdm.py`, `eval/evaluate_ar.py`, `eval/evaluate_mdm.py` and
  `scripts/prepare_slimpajama.py` derive from it, as do the model-size ladder and
  the training hyperparameters.

* TinyLlama (Zhang et al., 2024), https://github.com/jzhang38/TinyLlama, and
  lit-gpt / litgpt (Lightning AI), https://github.com/Lightning-AI/litgpt,
  Apache-2.0.
  `lit_gpt/` (model, config, packed_dataset, tokenizer, speed_monitor, utils,
  rmsnorm, fused_cross_entropy, fused_rotary_embedding) derives from these, via
  SMDM. The pretraining tokenizer is TinyLlama's.

* nanoGPT (Karpathy, 2022), https://github.com/karpathy/nanoGPT, MIT.
  The training loop and the cosine learning-rate schedule derive from it, via
  lit-gpt.

The methods this study implements and compares are described in:
BD3LM, "Block Diffusion" (Arriola et al., 2025); E2D2 (Arriola et al., 2026);
and DUEL (Turok et al., 2026).


